\section{Module 1: Horizon Dashboard \& Core Services Lifecycle}

\subsection{Objective \& Exploration}
Module 1 verifies the initial operational state of the deployed OpenStack platform. It establishes baseline functionality across compute, storage, and networking layers through both the Horizon graphical user interface and the OpenStack unified CLI.

\subsection{Core Services Inspection}
Upon authentication to the Horizon dashboard under the \texttt{demo} project context, all core resource catalogs were inspected:

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\begin{minipage}{0.49\linewidth}
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{img/m1-compute-resource-overview.png}
    \caption{Horizon Compute Overview and quotas.}
    \label{fig:m1_overview}
\end{minipage}\hfill
\begin{minipage}{0.49\linewidth}
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{img/m1-glance-image-catalog.png}
    \caption{Glance cloud base image repository.}
    \label{fig:m1_glance_images}
\end{minipage}
\end{figure}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Compute Overview (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_overview}):} Validated project quota limits (10 Instances, 20 vCPUs, 50 GiB RAM, 1000 GiB Volume Storage, and 50 Floating IPs).
    \item \textbf{Image Catalog (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_glance_images}):} Glance registered two base images: lightweight \nolinkurl{cirros-0.6.3-x86_64-disk} (20.69 MB) for rapid diagnostic testing and \nolinkurl{Fedora-Cloud-Base-37-1.7} (470 MB) for full Linux workloads.
    \item \textbf{Network Infrastructure (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_networks}):} Default DevStack networking was verified, including internal tenant networks (\texttt{private}, \texttt{shared}, \texttt{heat-net}) and external provider network (\texttt{public}).
    \item \textbf{Subnet Addressing (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_subnets}):} Detailed inspection of \texttt{private-net} verified dual-stack IPv4 (\nolinkurl{10.0.0.0/26}) and IPv6 (\nolinkurl{fd52:aee0:36f2::/64}) configuration.
\end{itemize}

