\subsection{Instance Lifecycle: Launch, Verification, and Deprovisioning}
To validate end-to-end VM scheduling, an ephemeral instance named \nolinkurl{module1-horizon-instance} was launched via the Horizon multi-step wizard (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_launch_dialog}):
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Parameters:} Flavor \texttt{m1.nano} (1 vCPU, 64 MB RAM, 1 GB Disk), Source \nolinkurl{cirros-0.6.3-x86_64-disk}, Network \texttt{private}.
    \item \textbf{Runtime Verification (Figure~\ref{fig:m1_instance_active}):} The instance attained \texttt{Active} status with power state \texttt{Running}, obtaining internal IP addresses \texttt{10.0.0.45} (IPv4) and \nolinkurl{fd52:aee0:36f2:0:f816:3eff:fed0:3caa} (IPv6).
    \item \textbf{Deprovisioning Flow (Figures~\ref{fig:m1_delete_confirmation} and~\ref{fig:m1_instances_empty}):} The instance was terminated through the confirmation modal. The instance inventory returned to an empty state, confirming successful reclamation of compute quotas and virtual ports.
\end{itemize}

